/-! Generated by `scripts/proofgen_artifact.py`; do not edit.

# Instruction-address facts for the frozen artifact

The kernel walks `instructionList` (11461 entries behind 29 appended chunks)
linearly, so proofs must never reduce `artifact.instructionPC n`,
`located i` or `instructionList[n]` by evaluation. Instead:

* `instrTree` / `pcTree` are balanced binary lookup trees (bit-interleaved
  indexing) holding every instruction and every byte offset, generated from
  the artifact by `define_tables`.
* `tables_ok` validates both trees against `instructionList` with ONE linear
  Boolean pass (`checkAll`), evaluated once by the kernel.
* `instrAt n` / `pcAt n` read the trees; `located_instruction_eq` and
  `instructionPC_eq_pcAt` connect them to `located` / `instructionPC`.
* `jumpdest_of n pc (by decide +kernel)` proves
  `Decode.isValidJumpDest optBytecode pc = true` for every JUMPDEST.
* Simprocs `instrAt_lit`, `pcAt_lit`, `instructionPC_lit`,
  `isValidJumpDest_lit` (the instruction data is read once per process and
  cached).
-/

namespace MlDsaOpt65.Proofs.Infra

open EvmSemantics
